alter table screenshot_uploads add column order_timestamp timestamptz;

comment on column screenshot_uploads.order_timestamp is 'Story P2-2 prerequisite — the order''s actual date/time as printed on the receipt/confirmation screenshot (distinct from created_at, which is upload time and can lag the real order by hours or days). Nullable: resolved via a regex-first pass over the OCR text (lib/orderTimestamp.js, targeting common receipt formats — see that file''s header) with a model-call fallback only on the two full parse paths (screenshotParser.js''s text/image branches, not the cheaper dictionary-hit items-only call — see that file''s comment for why), and left null rather than fabricated when neither resolves, per this pipeline''s established "never guess" convention (merchant/category follow the same rule). Known imprecision: parsed without account timezone context (screenshotParser.js has no account/timezone parameter) — stored as the literal printed wall-clock numbers interpreted as UTC, not localized. lib/preferenceProfile.js''s day-of-week histogram deliberately excludes rows where this is null from that specific signal (they still count normally for category/merchant) rather than silently falling back to created_at, since upload time is not a reliable proxy for order day.';
